{"type": "vertex_text", "round": 1, "text": "I have completed a full source-fidelity and internal consistency review of the entire patent application draft. The review traced every claim limitation, numbered part, and structural or functional assertion in the description and figure briefs to the affirmative inventor disclosure in `input/disclosure.md` and `input/conversation.md`. The review also checked for internal consistency across all draft files.\n\nWhile the core technical disclosure is well-supported by the inventor's source material, I found three critical inconsistencies between the figure briefs (`figures/*.md`), the numeral lists within those briefs, and the main text of the application (`draft/07-drawings.md` and `draft/08-detailed-description.md`). These inconsistencies would lead to drawings that contradict the numbering scheme and the textual description of the figures. The provided fixes resolve these contradictions by ensuring that each figure brief only describes parts that are intended to be numbered and referenced in that specific figure, bringing the drawing instructions into alignment with the rest of the application."}
